sentences.l:
Then in turn Sarpedon missed with his shining spear,
and over Patroclus’ left shoulder went the tip
of the spear, and he did not hit him;

And he fell, as when an oak falls, or a white poplar,
or a tall pine, which on the mountains builders
cut down with newly sharpened axes, to be ship-timber;

For a wound I have, this strong one, and about me my hand
with sharp pains has been driven, and not to me the blood
can dry, and my shoulder is heavy under it;

“Hector, now indeed wholly forgetful you are of the allies,
who for your sake far from their friends and native land
are wasting away their life;

So he spoke, and the Trojans from the head down seized grief,
unrestrainable, not yielding, since for them a prop of the city
he was, even a foreigner though being;
